course: dictionary
lesson: 9005
title: Skilful: good because of practice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Skilful means very good at doing something, and it usually comes from practice and ability. A skilful builder lays bricks straight and neat. A skilful player controls the ball well. Look for clues in the words around it.
explain: «English borrowed gauche to mean clumsy and adroit (from à droit) to mean skilful.» The sentence sets two words side by side: clumsy and skilful. Clumsy means awkward and careless, so skilful must mean the opposite: very good at doing something.
explain: «Columbus was a brave, skilful sailor but also a harsh governor who enslaved native people.» The word but is the clue. It shows two different sides of one person. Skilful describes one thing he was good at, sailing. It does not mean he was good in every way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «a very good sailor» in place of «a skilful sailor». If it still makes sense and keeps the same feeling, you have the right meaning.
fact: Skilful means very good at doing something because of practice and ability.
fact: Skilfully is the adverb: something done in a skilful way is done with great skill.
fact: British English spells it skilful; American English spells it skillful.
fact: Clumsy is the opposite of skilful.
fact: Being skilful usually comes from practice, not just talent.
exercise: «English borrowed gauche to mean clumsy and adroit to mean skilful.» What does adroit mean here? | *Skilful | Tired | Loud | Lost
exercise: Which word means the opposite of skilful? | *clumsy | brave | governor | sailor
exercise: «Columbus was a brave, skilful sailor but also a harsh governor.» What does the word but tell us? | *He had two sides: he was good at sailing but did harm in other ways | It is a question | Skilful means harsh | He was the same in every way
test: «She played the violin with skilful fingers, and every note was clear.» What does skilful describe here? | Being very loud on stage | *Being very good at playing the violin | Being very tired after practice
test: Being skilful usually comes from what? | Being rich | Being the tallest in the class | *Practice and ability | Luck alone
exam: Which sentence uses skilful correctly? | *The skilful builder laid each brick straight and neat. | The skilful rain fell on the cat. | The skilful table was very hungry. | Skilfully is a noun for a cup.
